8- What is the difference between run and go commands?
run: used to execture the command stored in u-boot env variable
go: jumps to address in RAM and execute code directly

9- What is the purpose of bootargs and who reads it?
they are kernel command line arguements, which tells kernel how to start up, it's read by kernel before init process runs to configure its behavior. it helps define console device and root filesystem

10- Why do we use 0x62000000 and not 0x60000000 for kernel address on Raspberry Pi?
because U-boot, DTB are typically sitting at 0x60000000, so we choose 0x62000000 to avoid overlapping with them. Thus we ensure the kernel has a contiguous memory region for use
